PRD: AKWA IBOM RENTAL REVIEW & VERIFICATION PLATFORM
Working name: RentTruth AKS (change anytime)
Version 0.1 - Draft for founder review
==========================================================
1. OVERVIEW
----------------------------------------------------------
Renting a home in Uyo and the rest of Akwa Ibom is a trust problem. Tenants get shown one house and handed another ("what I ordered vs what I got"), pay agents who vanish, rent rooms that were already sold or let to someone else, and discover problems (flooding, no water, bad landlords, noisy compounds) only after paying. There is no shared memory: when a tenant moves out, everything they learned disappears.
THE PRODUCT: a social, community-driven web platform where tenants who are moving out upload real photos and honest reviews of the place they lived in, and where house hunters can check a property, landlord or agent BEFORE paying anything. Think of it as Airbnb reviews + Google Maps photos + a scam-watch board, built for the Akwa Ibom rental market.
NOTE ON SOURCES: this draft is based on well-known rental pain points in Nigerian cities and what the founder described. Before building, validate with 15 to 20 real conversations in Uyo (tenants, agents, landlords) and collect local numbers (typical rent, agent fees, scam reports). No statistics have been invented here.
2. PROBLEM STATEMENT
----------------------------------------------------------
- Misrepresentation: photos online or on WhatsApp don't match the real house; a different house is shown at inspection.
- Agent fraud: inspection fees, "commitment" fees or rent collected, then the agent is unreachable.
- Double letting / already sold: the same room or building is rented to multiple people, or the property is already sold/occupied.
- Hidden defects: flooding, bad drainage, no water, poor power, leaking roof, insecurity, noisy neighbours.
- Landlord issues: sudden rent hikes, unfair deductions, harassment, refusal to repair.
- Unregulated agent fees: agent, agreement and legal fees vary wildly with no benchmark.
- No accountability: a bad agent or landlord simply changes number and continues.
3. GOALS AND NON-GOALS
----------------------------------------------------------
GOALS
- Let any tenant or house hunter see honest, photo-backed reviews of a property, landlord or agent before paying.
- Make outgoing tenants the source of truth by making it quick and rewarding to post a move-out review.
- Reduce scams by building public, verifiable reputations for agents and landlords.
- Become the first place people in Uyo check before paying any rent or fee.
NON-GOALS (for MVP)
- Not handling rent payments or escrow yet (Phase 3).
- Not a legal dispute service.
- Not covering all of Nigeria. Launch Uyo first, then expand across Akwa Ibom (Eket, Ikot Ekpene, Oron, Abak, Ikot Abasi) and beyond.
4. TARGET USERS
----------------------------------------------------------
1. Outgoing tenant (the contributor): moving out, has the best knowledge of the place. Motivation: help the next person, vent fairly, get recognition, possibly rewards.
2. House hunter (the reader): students (UNIUYO, AKSU), young professionals, civil servants, families, newly posted workers, people relocating from other states. Motivation: avoid scams and bad houses.
3. Honest agent: wants to stand out from scammers and get more clients through a verified badge.
4. Landlord / property owner: wants good tenants and to defend their reputation with replies.
5. Admin / moderator: verifies listings, handles reports and disputes.
5. CORE CONCEPT: THE MOVE-OUT REVIEW
----------------------------------------------------------
A guided 3 to 5 minute flow a tenant completes while packing out:
1. Confirm the property (map pin + address + house photo).
2. Upload photos by checklist: compound and gate, sitting room, bedrooms, kitchen, bathroom/toilet, ceiling and roof leaks, water source, meter, drainage, street at the front.
3. Rate categories (1 to 5): water, light/power, security, drainage and flooding, neighbours, landlord behaviour, value for money, agent honesty.
4. Write or record (voice note) the "I loved this / I didn't like this" summary.
5. Add the facts: rent paid, period, agent fee paid, caution fee, whether rent was increased, and whether the deposit was returned.
6. Answer: Would you rent here again? Would you recommend this agent/landlord?
7. Submit. Photos are timestamped and geotagged for credibility.
6. BEST-CASE SCENARIOS (what great looks like)
----------------------------------------------------------
- Chioma, a nurse posted to Uyo, searches an area, finds a flat with 6 move-out reviews, real photos and a note that the compound floods in heavy rain. She skips it and finds a better one with a verified landlord.
- A student checks a hostel room before paying and sees the real bathroom photos, noting the water is borehole-supplied and reliable. She pays confidently.
- An honest agent earns a Verified badge and 40 positive reviews. Clients now come to him by name, and he stops competing on price alone.
- A good landlord replies to a review, fixes the leaking roof, and updates his listing. His property fills faster and he can charge fairly.
- A moving-out tenant posts a review in five minutes, earns a "Trusted Reviewer" badge and credits that can be used for perks.
- A scam attempt is stopped when a house hunter searches the agent's phone number, finds three scam reports and warns friends in the community.
- The state benefits: aggregated data shows where housing is poor and where prices are fair, which is valuable to planners, banks and developers.
7. WORST-CASE SCENARIOS AND MITIGATIONS
----------------------------------------------------------
* Fake positive reviews by agents/landlords
  Risk: platform loses trust.
  Fix: require proof of tenancy (geotagged photos + phone verification + optional agreement/receipt); owners and agents cannot review their own property; spam and pattern detection; review limit per user per property.
* Fake negative reviews by rivals
  Risk: unfair damage to honest people.
  Fix: same proof rules; right of reply; report-and-review process; flagged reviews checked by a human.
* Defamation claims from landlords/agents
  Risk: legal exposure.
  Fix: reviews framed around factual experience; clear terms; no unverified criminal accusations stated as fact (use "reported by users"); takedown and dispute process; have a Nigerian lawyer review the terms.
* Tenants fear retaliation
  Risk: nobody posts.
  Fix: allow posting after move-out; allow pseudonymous display names (identity known only to admins); hide exact unit numbers if needed.
* Privacy breach
  Risk: faces, number plates, neighbours' details exposed.
  Fix: guidance not to photograph people; remove personal phone numbers from reviews; comply with the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023.
* Platform only has data for a few areas
  Risk: low value, people leave.
  Fix: seed Uyo area by area; reward early reviewers; collect field data through campus ambassadors.
* Scammers list fake properties on the platform
  Risk: becomes a new scam channel.
  Fix: listings require verification (phone, ID, physical check for badge); "Unverified" clearly labelled; no in-app payments in the MVP.
* Poor internet / low data
  Risk: people can't upload photos.
  Fix: image compression, resumable uploads, lightweight pages, PWA with offline draft saving.
* Mob behaviour / harassment
  Risk: toxic community.
  Fix: community guidelines, moderation, report buttons, rate limits.
* Landlords and agents oppose the platform
  Risk: resistance, threats.
  Fix: position as "fair for good landlords"; give them verified badges and a right of reply.
* Low contribution (cold start)
  Risk: empty site.
  Fix: start with reviews collected by the team; partner with student bodies and estate groups; reward the first 500 reviewers.
