9. KEY USER FLOWS
----------------------------------------------------------
FLOW A - Check before you pay: open site > search area or paste agent number/address > see property page > read reviews and photos > see scam flags > share or contact verified party.
FLOW B - Post a move-out review: sign in > tap "I'm moving out" > pick or add property > guided photo checklist > ratings and facts > submit > review goes live after automated checks (and human check if flagged).
FLOW C - Report a scam: tap report > choose type (fake listing, collected money and vanished, double letting, misrepresentation) > add phone/name/evidence > submit > admin reviews > shown as "reported by N users" once threshold and review criteria are met.
FLOW D - Landlord/agent reply: receive notification > verify identity > post public reply > optionally update listing or mark issue as fixed.
10. TRUST AND VERIFICATION SYSTEM
----------------------------------------------------------
This is what makes or breaks the product.
1. Phone-verified accounts (OTP) for every user.
2. Proof of tenancy (any one of: geotagged photos taken at the property, tenancy agreement, rent receipt, utility bill). Reviews with proof get a "Verified Tenant" tag and rank higher.
3. Photo integrity: capture timestamp and location metadata; flag reused images (duplicate image detection).
4. Anti-abuse: one review per tenant per tenancy, rate limits, owner/agent self-review blocks.
5. Reputation scores for reviewers, agents and landlords, weighted by verified reviews.
6. Transparency: every property shows how many reviews are verified and the date of the last review (old reviews count less).
7. Dispute process: the reviewed party can contest; a moderator checks evidence; outcomes are logged.
11. DATA MODEL (high level)
----------------------------------------------------------
- User: id, phone, display name, role(s), verification level, reputation points.
- Property: id, address, coordinates, area, type, photos, current status, owner link (optional).
- Review: id, property id, user id, tenancy dates, rent paid, fees paid, category ratings, text/voice, photos, proof, status, verified flag.
- Agent / Landlord profile: id, name, phones, verification status, linked properties, average rating, scam report count.
- ScamReport: id, reported phone/name, type, evidence, reporter id, status, review notes.
- Reply, Comment, Report, Badge, Notification.
12. MONETIZATION (later, never at the cost of trust)
----------------------------------------------------------
- Verified badge subscription for agents and landlords (they pay for verification work, not for good reviews).
- Featured verified listings (clearly labelled).
- Inspection booking and lead fees from verified agents.
- Escrow / payment transaction fee (Phase 3).
- Anonymised market data reports for banks, developers and institutions.
- Reviewer rewards funded by the above (airtime, data, discount partners).
RULE: no one can pay to remove or hide a genuine review.
13. LEGAL, PRIVACY AND SAFETY
----------------------------------------------------------
- Consult a Nigerian lawyer on defamation risk, terms of use and takedown process before launch.
- Comply with the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023: clear consent, privacy policy, data minimisation, secure storage.
- Avoid publishing sensitive personal data; mask phone numbers in reviews (Scam Check search can still match them).
- Language: show "reported by users" rather than declaring someone a criminal.
- Make it easy for any person to request correction or removal of inaccurate content.
- Consider engaging the Akwa Ibom State ministry responsible for housing/lands and local estate or landlord associations early, so the platform is seen as a partner.
14. GO-TO-MARKET (Uyo first)
----------------------------------------------------------
1. Seed the data: the team (or paid campus ambassadors) documents 100 properties across 10 popular Uyo neighbourhoods; collect 200+ tenant reviews.
2. Campus launch: UNIUYO, AKSU and other schools. Students move every year and are heavy WhatsApp users.
3. WhatsApp and social: shareable review cards, a community group, TikTok/Instagram/X short videos of "what I ordered vs what I got" stories.
4. Estate and church/community groups: trusted channels in Akwa Ibom.
5. Honest agents first: onboard 20 to 30 good agents as early partners and badge them.
6. Local media and influencers: campaign around "Check before you pay."
7. Reviewer rewards: airtime or data for the first 500 verified reviews.
