16. SUGGESTED TECH APPROACH
----------------------------------------------------------
- Frontend: Next.js / React as a mobile-first PWA (works like an app without app-store friction).
- Backend: Node.js (or Python/Django), PostgreSQL with PostGIS for location search.
- Storage: cloud image storage with automatic compression (Cloudinary, S3 or similar).
- Auth: phone OTP via a Nigerian-friendly SMS provider.
- Maps: Google Maps or OpenStreetMap/Mapbox.
- Moderation: admin dashboard plus basic automated checks (duplicate images, spam).
- Performance: lazy loading, image compression, light pages, resumable uploads for weak networks.
- Later: native Android app (most users are on Android), USSD or WhatsApp bot for low-data users.
17. ROADMAP
----------------------------------------------------------
Phase 0 - Research (Weeks 1-3): interviews, competitor review, legal consult, brand.
Phase 1 - MVP build (Weeks 4-12): reviews, property pages, Scam Check, search, moderation.
Phase 2 - Uyo pilot (Months 3-6): seed data, campus launch, first 500 reviews.
Phase 3 - Trust layer (Months 6-9): verified badges, ordered-vs-got view, community features.
Phase 4 - Marketplace (Months 9-15): verified listings, inspections, payment/escrow research.
Phase 5 - Expansion (Year 2): other Akwa Ibom towns, then other states.
18. KEY RISKS
----------------------------------------------------------
- Cold start: an empty platform has no value. Fix: seed data aggressively in a small area.
- Legal pushback. Fix: lawyer, careful wording, dispute process.
- Fake reviews. Fix: proof of tenancy and moderation.
- Low contribution. Fix: rewards, easy flow, voice notes.
- Data cost for users. Fix: lightweight design and compression.
- Funding. Fix: start lean, validate with the pilot, then pursue grants/angels interested in proptech and consumer protection.
